[17592186198361 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186493973 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198361 #edb/ref 1039 "Performing a Change of Variables" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198361 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186198235 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198361 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "9fed8ac2-8d21-5bc9-b1cc-df20760cfbfb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198373 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186198951 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198373 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186199007 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198373 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186373930 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198373 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186373937 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198373 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186373944 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198373 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186375516 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198373 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186481389 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198373 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186481418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198373 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186481432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198373 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186481434 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198373 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186495059 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198373 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186495100 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198373 #edb/ref 1039 "Cases When the Transformation Is Inferred From the Domain" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198373 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186198015 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198373 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "cd546dda-c78f-5367-b03e-9b3acb420040" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198374 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186198579 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198374 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186198596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198374 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186373916 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198374 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186373923 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198374 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186373951 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198374 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186373958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198374 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186481343 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198374 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186481364 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198374 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186481410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198374 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186481423 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198374 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186481430 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198374 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186501235 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198374 #edb/ref 1039 "Cases When the Transformation Is Inferred From the Integrand" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198374 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186198016 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198374 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "b2682751-23e4-5cf2-9a46-82c75765423f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198479 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198479 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198479 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198479 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198479 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198479 #edb/ref 1045 "Computing Double Integrals Using a Change of Variables" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198479 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186199250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198479 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050482 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198479 #edb/ref 1050 1020.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198479 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "8416c2c4-cff0-5744-94c6-6f83c5fc5709" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198596 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186194207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198596 #edb/ref 1069 "q-160896" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198596 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198596 #edb/ref 1071 "Use a change of variables to evaluate the double integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(2x-1)(x+y)^{2}\\,dxdy,\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the quadrilateral region with vertices $(1,0),$ $(2,-1),$ $(2,2),$ and $(1,3).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198596 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e243f9b4-c60d-5cd6-bd2d-b886dddad51a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198596 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dxdy={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v),y(u,v))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nThe integrand\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=(2x-1)(x+y)^{2}\n$$\n\nsuggests that we use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=2x-1,\\,v=x+y.\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nThe vertices of our domain $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}(1,0) & =(2(1)-1,1+0) \\\\  & =(1,1) \\\\ {T}^{-1}(2,-1) & =(2(2)-1,2+(-1)) \\\\  & =(3,1) \\\\ {T}^{-1}(2,2) & =(2(2)-1,2+2) \\\\  & =(3,4) \\\\ {T}^{-1}(1,3) & =(2(1)-1,1+3) \\\\  & =(1,4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our domain in the $uv$-plane is the following rectangle:\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 3,\\,1\\le v\\le 4\\}\n$$\n\n![](images/1d/1d5943d2cf79e7c77f6db3e939242d7e31068f46506fa618abd24b6ac813d32a.png)\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 5**: Perform the change of variables, and evaluate the integral:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(2x-1)(x+y)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{Δ}u{v}^{2}\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}u{v}^{2}\\,|\\frac{1}{2}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{3}u{v}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{v}^{2}\\text{d}v{\\int }_{1}^{3}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}{v}^{3}]}_{1}^{4}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}]}_{1}^{3}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 21\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =42.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199250 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199250 #edb/ref 1061 26976 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199250 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5a4dcbdc-b666-5ac5-82b5-d1e2d96f958e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199250 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186199451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199251 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199251 #edb/ref 1061 26978 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199251 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "38215948-f2f7-5757-b967-2b0aad077150" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199251 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198361 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199273 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199273 #edb/ref 1061 44170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199273 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "418d8ff2-cd87-5ef1-b69c-c511c7c5b360" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199273 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198373 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199274 #edb/ref 1061 44171 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199274 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e9c97e5e-4063-57fd-b261-2a276cea9f27" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199274 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198374 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199451 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose that \n\n$$\n\\mathbf T: (u,v) \\to \\left(x(u,v),y(u,v)\\right)\n$$\n\nis a $C^1$ transformation that has no critical points (i.e., it is invertible) inside some region $\\Delta\\subset \\mathbb R^2,$ and that $\\mathbf T(\\Delta) = D,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/66/668b8a0dae060c7929b92c6abe3601b0ede0b8444d92f33f4a8b5627410a4447.png)\n\n \n\nWe've already seen how the area of a non-trivial region $D$ can be computed using the change of variables formula:\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{D} \\mathrm d x \\mathrm d y = \\iint\\limits_{\\Delta} \\left| \\dfrac{\\partial (x, y)}{\\partial (u, v)} \\right|  \\ \\mathrm d u \\mathrm d v\n$$\n\nWe can extend this formula to compute the integral of a function $f(x,y)$ over $D,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{D} f(x,y) \\ \\mathrm d x \\mathrm d y = \\iint\\limits_{\\Delta} \\ f(x(u,v), y(u,v)) \\:  \\left| \\dfrac{\\partial (x, y)}{\\partial (u, v)} \\right|  \\ \\mathrm d u \\mathrm d v\n$$\n\nNote the similarity with the change of variables formula for the integral of a single-variable function $f(x)$ over $D = (a,b){:}$\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_D f(x)\\,\\textrm d x = \\int\\limits_{\\Delta} f(x(u))\\,\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d u}\\, \\textrm d u\n$$\n\nApplying the change of variables formula is similar to when we were restricting our attention to areas in the plane. The only difference now is that we must also express the integrand $f(x,y)$ in terms of $u$ and $v.$\n\nLet's see an example." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199451 #edb/ref 1065 4402 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199451 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "2fb63b1e-64c3-58e1-94d8-3d7a87445cd7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199451 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493410 #edb/ref 1080 "3({e}^{-1/2}-{e}^{-2})\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493410 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493410 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0b6b5fe5-29d1-5793-a274-fa3b5699e913" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493432 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{e}{8}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493432 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493432 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "17dcff5e-6574-5e2e-be4c-22c67c1a31d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493554 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{e}^{-1}-{e}^{-2}}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493554 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493554 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "702b0bc2-ac10-5437-9f18-9fa877532a9e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493601 #edb/ref 1080 "8{e}^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493601 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493601 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "857734df-e10d-5568-a049-4e87b8b5c0d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493747 #edb/ref 1080 "({e}^{2}-e)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493747 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493747 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e162164d-9035-55fa-9f1c-b47ea0bae241" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493808 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493808 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493808 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493554 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493808 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493601 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493808 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493747 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493808 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493808 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493808 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186493410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493808 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "15ea503e-c96f-567a-8f89-cf26cc3e1193" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493956 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186493808 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493956 #edb/ref 1069 "q-160899" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493956 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493956 #edb/ref 1071 "Using the change of variables $u=\\frac{y}{x}$ and $v=xy,$ evaluate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}{e}^{-xy/2}\\,dx\\,dy,\n$$\n\nwhere $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{x}{4}\\le y\\le 2x,\\,1\\le xy\\le 4\\}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493956 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c5c02db8-6f5e-5ac6-a24e-9e9016b1082e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493956 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v),y(u,v))|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|du\\,dv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{y}{x},\\,v=xy\n$$\n\n \ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uv$-plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\le u\\le 2,\\,1\\le v\\le 4\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} & \\frac{1}{x} \\\\ y & \\text{ }\\text{ }x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-\\frac{2y}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{(-\\frac{2y}{x})}=-\\frac{1}{2u}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{e}^{-xy/2}\\,dx\\,dy & ={∬}_{Δ}{e}^{-v/2}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}{e}^{-v/2}\\cdot |-\\frac{1}{2u}|\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{1/4}^{2}\\frac{{e}^{-v/2}}{u}\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{e}^{-v/2}[{\\int }_{1/4}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u]\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{e}^{-v/2}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|\\,{|}_{1/4}^{2}]du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{e}^{-v/2}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{1}{4}]\\,du \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{e}^{-v/2}\\,du \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}\\cdot {[-2{e}^{-v/2}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot ({e}^{-2}-{e}^{-1/2}) \\\\  & =3({e}^{-1/2}-{e}^{-2})\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494431 #edb/ref 1080 "3-4\\pi " #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494431 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494431 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "36ad6cac-d25a-50df-a71c-ff5530463782" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494433 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{3}{2\\pi }" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494433 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 1