 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494880 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ebf26341-3745-5f43-a14c-cda67d69e390" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494987 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494570 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494987 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494600 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494987 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494987 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494739 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494987 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494880 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494987 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494987 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494987 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186494608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494987 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "91b5b4ea-2fbf-58c6-b385-fcfece3b9311" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495012 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494431 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495012 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494433 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495012 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494436 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495012 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494571 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495012 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494723 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495012 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495012 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495012 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186494571 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495012 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "caaee621-928c-5865-8689-d0a675bcc7ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495059 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494987 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495059 #edb/ref 1069 "q-160917" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495059 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495059 #edb/ref 1071 "Use a change of variables to evaluate the double integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{y-2x}{y+2x}\\,dxdy,\n$$\n\nwhere $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y-2x\\le 2,\\,2\\le y+2x\\le 6\\}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495059 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "11be1c1c-7eab-52eb-aab8-c16c55806ef6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495059 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dxdy={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v),y(u,v))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nThe inequalities that define the region $D,$\n\n$$\n0\\le y-2x\\le 2,\\,2\\le y+2x\\le 6,\n$$\n\nsuggest that we use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=y-2x\\,\\text{and}\\,v=y+2x.\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uv$-plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,2\\le v\\le 6\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ \\text{ }\\text{ }\\text{ }2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 5**: Perform the change of variables, and evaluate the integral:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{y-2x}{y+2x}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{Δ}\\frac{u}{v}\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}\\frac{u}{v}|-\\frac{1}{4}|\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}u[{\\int }_{2}^{6}\\frac{1}{v}\\,dv]du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}u[\\operatorname{ln}⁡|v|]_{2}^{6}\\,du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}u(\\operatorname{ln}⁡6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)\\,du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}u\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,du \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{4}{[\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495100 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186495012 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495100 #edb/ref 1069 "q-160915" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495100 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495100 #edb/ref 1071 "Use a change of variables to evaluate the double integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi xy)\\,dxdy,\n$$\n\nwhere $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le xy\\le 4,\\,1\\le \\frac{y}{x}\\le 5\\}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495100 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "75903bf3-d1b7-5813-a3cf-49663583fcbd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495100 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dxdy={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v),y(u,v))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nThe inequalities that define the region $D,$\n\n$$\n1\\le xy\\le 4,\\,1\\le \\frac{y}{x}\\le 5,\n$$\n\nsuggest that we use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=xy\\,\\text{and}\\,v=\\frac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uv$-plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 4,\\,1\\le v\\le 5\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}\\text{ }\\text{ }\\text{ }y & x \\\\ -\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} & \\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{(\\frac{2y}{x})}=\\frac{1}{2v}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 5**: Perform the change of variables, and evaluate the integral:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi xy)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{D}{(\\frac{y}{x})}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi xy)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}{v}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi u)|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}{v}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi u)|\\frac{1}{2v}|\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi u)[{\\int }_{1}^{5}v\\,dv]du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi u){[\\frac{1}{2}\\,{v}^{2}]}_{1}^{5}\\,du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi u)\\cdot 12\\,du \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi u)\\,du \\\\  & =6{[-\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi u)]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{\\pi }(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{12}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500462 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186501255 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500462 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186501274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500462 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186501286 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500462 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186501290 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500462 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186501295 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500462 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500462 #edb/ref 1045 "Computing Double Integrals Using a Change of Variables" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500462 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186501274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500462 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500462 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050482 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500462 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "5fa958b3-5d69-501f-b05b-9c4db4f578a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500621 #edb/ref 1080 "1-\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500621 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500621 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4c949071-0d3c-54bb-9dc4-96b0d8539778" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500665 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{4}-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500665 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500665 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "610bdf54-043a-5740-ad3a-0dec8d2b57b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500680 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500680 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500680 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "663bf8f7-c948-5768-ae58-7d976d853146" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500911 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500911 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500911 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cee0c053-9570-5242-9c89-c00687d42bb7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500939 #edb/ref 1080 "4({e}^{2}-1)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500939 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500939 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dde36f82-c9e7-56b6-95a2-ab881de27e91" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501105 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501105 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501105 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501105 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500911 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501105 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500939 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501105 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501105 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501105 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186500939 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501105 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "bb9e74ba-160b-54c7-b340-b16d836e9f06" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501235 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501105 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501235 #edb/ref 1069 "q-160895" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501235 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501235 #edb/ref 1071 "Use a change of variables to evaluate the double integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(x-y){e}^{x+y}\\,dxdy,\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the quadrilateral region with vertices $(0,0),$ $(2,-2),$ $(3,-1),$ and $(1,1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501235 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ea3ea5b4-3a71-55fd-af96-eb417a578734" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501235 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dxdy={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v),y(u,v))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nThe integrand\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=(x-y){e}^{x+y}\n$$\n\nsuggests that we use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=x-y,\\,v=x+y.\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nThe vertices of our domain $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}(0,0) & =(0-0,0+0) \\\\  & =(0,0) \\\\ {T}^{-1}(2,-2) & =(2-(-2),2+(-2)) \\\\  & =(4,0) \\\\ {T}^{-1}(3,-1) & =(3-(-1),3+(-1)) \\\\  & =(4,2) \\\\ {T}^{-1}(1,1) & =(1-1,1+1) \\\\  & =(0,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our domain in the $uv$-plane is the following rectangle:\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 4,\\,0\\le v\\le 2\\}\n$$\n\n![](images/0b/0b23c6463447aa1fb64bdeeca689a40711f8dad59b348bb7943c2b9d2de7e8fc.png)\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & \\text{ }\\text{ }1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 5**: Perform the change of variables, and evaluate the integral:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(x-y){e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{Δ}u{e}^{v}\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}u{e}^{v}\\,|\\frac{1}{2}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}u{e}^{v}\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{v}\\,\\text{d}v{\\int }_{0}^{4}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot [{e}^{v}]_{0}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}]}_{0}^{4}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot ({e}^{2}-1)\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =4({e}^{2}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501255 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186501295 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501255 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1e5d6fdb-4349-5a22-9a20-57fac957a381" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501255 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501274 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186501255 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501274 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "72afaacc-fe08-5eba-992e-2a5c13b48917" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501274 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186501235 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501286 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b7040396-b7ee-5a68-99f5-cbdc7c619831" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501286 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186495059 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501290 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186501286 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501290 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c69702c1-10b7-5ba2-9e9f-d73b85226694" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501290 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186495100 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501295 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186501290 #edb/ref 17592186045417] 